  "description": "Post-surrealism is a movement that arose in Southern California in 1934 when Helen Lundeberg and Lorser Feitelson wrote a manifesto explaining their desire to use art to convey the relationship between the perceptual and the conceptual.\n\nThe term \"Post-surrealism\" is sometimes used to refer to art movements related to or influenced by Surrealism, which occurred after the period of \"historical surrealism\" of the 1920s and 30s.",
